    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only concrete test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), so the full suite is those 2 tests \u2014 both green, **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented locality derivation from city on the `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `locality` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits it on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/LocalityLookup.java`** (new) \u2014 A small static utility holding the fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) whose `forCity(String)` returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (including for a null city).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(...LocalityLookup.forCity(owner.getCity()))\")`, consistent with how `membershipTier`/`displayName` are derived in the mapper.\n\n**Key pitfall caught and fixed:** My first attempt put `deriveLocality(String)` as a `default` method *on the mapper interface*. MapStruct auto-adopted it as an implicit `String\u2192String` conversion and silently ran **every** string field (firstName, telephone, \u2026) through it \u2014 turning `telephone` into `\"UNKNOWN\"` and breaking owner creation with a 400. Moving the lookup into a standalone static utility referenced by a fully-qualified expression avoids MapStruct picking it up as a mapping method.\n\nThe derivation is a mapper-level projection from `city` (no new DB column), matching the test's ground truth exactly (case-sensitive lookup, `\"UNKNOWN\"` fallback).",
